From c9e3e2fe884cc5bda0a367d2cae83de588fe2144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 01:05:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] input: usb_kbd_hid: ignore non-keyboard reports from the
 composite HID device

This is a composite HID device: keyboard (Report ID 1), mouse (2),
consumer control (3), and gamepad (4) are all multiplexed over the
same interrupt endpoint (pocket-reform-keyboard-fw
usb_descriptors.h). usb_kbd_poll() never checked the Report ID before
scanning bytes [3:7] as keycodes, so a mouse or consumer-control
report interleaved with a real keypress read as all-zero keycode
bytes, i.e. "no keys pressed", releasing the key almost immediately
after it was detected.

Fix: ignore any report that isn't Report ID 1 before scanning it.

Also replace the long-commented-out raw printk dump of the report
bytes with a proper dev_dbg() using the same format, and add a
comment on the existing idle-resend memcmp check explaining why it's
needed (usb_set_idle() makes the device auto-resend its current
report every ~4ms even when nothing changed).

Signed-off-by: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
---
 drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c b/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
index b8119e09f4..a416380866 100644
--- a/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
+++ b/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
@@ -114,19 +114,30 @@ static void usb_kbd_poll(void *arg)
 		goto exit;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * This is a composite HID device: keyboard (Report ID 1), mouse (2),
+	 * consumer control (3), and gamepad (4) are all multiplexed over
+	 * this same interrupt endpoint (pocket-reform-keyboard-fw
+	 * usb_descriptors.h). A non-keyboard report interleaved with a real
+	 * keypress would otherwise get scanned as if it were keyboard data,
+	 * reading zeros at [3:7] and looking like every key just released.
+	 * Ignore anything that isn't Report ID 1 entirely.
+	 */
+	if (data->new[0] != 1)
+		goto exit;
+
+	/*
+	 * usb_set_idle() makes the device auto-resend its current report
+	 * every ~4ms even when nothing changed. Only scan on a real change,
+	 * otherwise this fires nonstop at idle.
+	 */
 	if (!memcmp(data->old, data->new, USB_KBD_BOOT_REPORT_SIZE))
 		goto exit;
 
-	/*printk(KERN_ALERT "%s: %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x\n", __func__,
-				 data->new[0], // 0x01
-				 data->new[1],
-				 data->new[2],
-				 data->new[3], // first key
-				 data->new[4],
-				 data->new[5],
-				 data->new[6],
-				 data->new[7]
-				 );*/
+	dev_dbg(&usbdev->dev, "ret=%d change: %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x\n",
+		ret,
+		data->new[0], data->new[1], data->new[2], data->new[3],
+		data->new[4], data->new[5], data->new[6], data->new[7]);
 
 	for (i = 3; i <= 7; i++) {
 		uint8_t pressed_new = data->new[i];
-- 
